# Golden CUDA source is compared byte-for-byte against the emitter's LF output
# (`include_str!` in the contraction byte-identity tests). The emitter always
# writes '\n'; force these goldens to LF on checkout so byte-identity holds on
# Windows too (autocrlf would otherwise convert them to CRLF and fail the test).
#
# Carried over from the Baracuda workspace. The original rule named
# crates/baracuda-kernelgen/src/goldens/*.cu; after the CUDA emitter was carved
# into baracuda-cuda-emit the goldens went WITH it, so that path matches nothing
# here and the protection silently did not apply -- the 32 .cu harnesses under
# ondevice/ landed as CRLF on the first cut and had to be renormalized.
#
# Match every .cu in the workspace instead of one directory, so a future
# relocation cannot quietly drop the guarantee again.
*.cu text eol=lf
